            <ArticleTitle>Aortocoronary endothelial cell-seeded polytetrafluoroethylene graft: 9-year patency.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1166-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a 71-year old man with coronary artery disease. Complete coronary revascularization was not possible with autologous grafts; therefore, a 4-mm expanded polytetrafluoroethylene graft was implanted that had been seeded preoperatively with autologous vascular endothelial cells. At 9-year follow-up, the patient is asymptomatic and shows a patent graft.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
